  <p>
    Most disappointment with SEO and ads isn’t Google being broken — it’s a mismatch between what an
    owner was promised and how long this actually takes. Across our accounts, meaningful growth has
    landed somewhere between <strong>two months and three years</strong> depending on where the
    company started. Here are the real timeframes, so you can judge your own situation against
    something other than a sales pitch.
  </p>

  <h2>What growth actually looked like, by account</h2>
  <p>
    These are our four case studies, with the honest elapsed time rather than the headline number:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Company</th>
        <th>Starting point</th>
        <th>Where it got to</th>
        <th>How long</th>
      </tr>
